# Dev Notes 10 — runtime-lifecycle-modularization-v1 request settlement helper

## Branch

`runtime-lifecycle-modularization-v1-request-settlement-helper`

## Status

First request-settlement helper slice staged, sandbox/mock verified, packaged, and locally real-runtime verified with one non-reproduced shutdown-timeout caveat.

This branch intentionally extracts only mechanically safe parent-side request completion/error settlement helpers. It does not move cancellation loops, lifecycle state, reset/shutdown coordination, init coordination, scheduler ownership, worker behavior, or public API behavior.

## Source base

Started from the current `modularization` branch source mirrored by:

```text
runtime-dev-repo-modularization.zip
```

The source base already included the first clean modularization slice:

```text
nativeOperationPolicy.mjs
docs/dev-notes.09
```

## Purpose

Continue lifecycle modularization conservatively by extracting request completion/error settlement primitives from `inference.mjs` into a small parent-side helper module.

The goal is to improve separation of concerns without changing runtime behavior.

## Implementation summary

Added:

```text
runtimeRequestSettlement.mjs
```

The new module owns only parent-side request settlement primitives:

```js
export function resolvePromptResult(req, msg) { ... }
export function closeRequestCancelChannel(req) { ... }
export function settleCompletedRequest(req, msg, deps) { ... }
export function settleFailedRequest(req, err, deps) { ... }
```

`inference.mjs` now imports:

```js
import {
    settleCompletedRequest,
    settleFailedRequest
} from "./runtimeRequestSettlement.mjs";
```

The worker `done` message path still owns scheduler completion in `inference.mjs`:

```js
const req = scheduler.complete(msg.id);
if (!req) return;

settleCompletedRequest(req, msg, {
    closeStream,
    traceDone,
    traceDelete
});
```

The worker request-level `error` path still owns lifecycle/init/session special-case routing and scheduler failure in `inference.mjs`:

```js
const req = scheduler.fail(msg.id);
if (!req) return;

settleFailedRequest(req, err, {
    errorStream,
    traceError,
    traceDelete
});
```

## What intentionally stayed in `inference.mjs`

The following behavior-bearing paths remain inline:

```text
notifyRequestCancellationRequested()
notifyRequestsCancellationRequested()
cancelPrompt()
resetSession() cancellation loop
resetModel() cancellation loop
cancelRequestsForShutdown()
shutdown mode orchestration
init/ready lifecycle routing
session/model/shutdown waiter routing
scheduler.complete/fail/cancel/cancelAll/cancelBySession ownership
```

Reason:

- cancellation paths involve scheduler state, parent cancel-port notification, worker cancel messages, stream cancellation, trace mutation, and `done` rejection;
- those paths have subtle ordering differences;
- moving them should be a separate reviewed slice after this first helper extraction is stable.

## Behavior preservation notes

No intentional changes to:

```text
initModel()
ensureModelReady()
prompt()
cancelPrompt()
resetSession()
resetModel()
shutdownRuntime()
scheduler behavior
worker lifecycle/replacement
worker operation serialization
config override validation
retry/profile planning
stream shaping
prompt/output semantics
model identity/path policy
native operation timeout/unhealthy policy
```

The helper does not:

```text
import inference.mjs
own scheduler state
send worker messages
own lifecycle state
change public API exports
change worker files
change config files
```

The exact prompt result fallback was preserved:

```text
streaming request: use req.finalText when non-empty; otherwise msg.res ?? req.finalText
non-streaming request: use msg.res ?? req.finalText
```

The exact completed-request settlement order was preserved:

```text
closeStream(req)
closeRequestCancelChannel(req)
traceDone(req)
req.resolveDone(resultText)
traceDelete(req.id)
```

The exact failed-request settlement order was preserved:

```text
closeRequestCancelChannel(req)
traceError(req, err)
errorStream(req, err)
req.rejectDone(err)
traceDelete(req.id)
```

No `closeRequestCancelChannel()` call was added to cancellation paths in this branch.

